      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the pointer, but I believe d5e79eeba308 is a different fix. It corrected the dma_heap_get_name() docs and removed the duplicated copies from include/linux/dma-heap.h, and that work is present in android-mainline today -- the \"Returns:\" block above dma_heap_get_name() came from it.\n\nWhat it didn\u0027t touch is the struct dma_heap member list, which is what this change is about: @heap_devt, @list, @heap_cdev and @heap_dev are missing the colon kernel-doc needs to associate them with a member, and @refcount isn\u0027t documented at all. On android-mainline at a7350f99bf23, before this change:\n\n  $ scripts/kernel-doc -none drivers/dma-buf/dma-heap.c\n  Warning: drivers/dma-buf/dma-heap.c:46 struct member \u0027heap_devt\u0027 not described in \u0027dma_heap\u0027\n  Warning: drivers/dma-buf/dma-heap.c:46 struct member \u0027list\u0027 not described in \u0027dma_heap\u0027\n  Warning: drivers/dma-buf/dma-heap.c:46 struct member \u0027heap_cdev\u0027 not described in \u0027dma_heap\u0027\n  Warning: drivers/dma-buf/dma-heap.c:46 struct member \u0027refcount\u0027 not described in \u0027dma_heap\u0027\n  Warning: drivers/dma-buf/dma-heap.c:46 struct member \u0027heap_dev\u0027 not described in \u0027dma_heap\u0027\n\n(the current script prints each of these twice, so the raw output is 10 lines for the 5 distinct warnings.)\n\nSo this looks like something that was simply never noticed, rather than a missing backport.",
