      "message": "Correction to my previous comment: the dma-heap.c half of d5e79eeba308 is in android-mainline, and so is the header dedup for dma_heap_get_drvdata() and dma_heap_add(). But the dma_heap_get_name() block you removed from include/linux/dma-heap.h is back, with the original incorrect wording:\n\n  /**\n   * dma_heap_get_name() - get heap name\n   * @heap: DMA-Heap to retrieve private data for\n   *\n   * Returns:\n   * The char* for the heap name.\n   */\n  const char *dma_heap_get_name(struct dma_heap *heap);\n\ndma-heap.c has your corrected \"retrieve the name of\", so the two have drifted apart again -- which is the exact duplication problem your commit removed. It sits next to the ANDROID-only dma_heap_get_dev() declaration; I couldn\u0027t identify which change reintroduced it from my tree. Out of scope for this change, but probably worth a separate look.",
